{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037372-omniscience-and-ways-of-achieving-it","id":1037372,"title":"Omniscience and ways of achieving it","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-24T12:48:51-08:00","id":1037372,"title":"Omniscience and ways of achieving it","content":"Recently we with one of my players discussed the construction of the setting with the assumption of extremely low population of magi. One of the common points where we have been agreed that in this case neophytes are themselves become a resource. Differing we attempt to answer whether the orders to compete with each other for newcomers? The answer to this question lies in the answer to another: Is it possible to detect the newly Awakened one? And there topic popup.<br /> Creating observational artifacts is not a big problem. Even if you make it a self-replicating. The problem is that it does not help to find a magician himself - only his Mojo (that's my point). My friend insisted that it would be enough to add to the design Fate arcane for increase the probability of detecting magick. Like, next to the sorcerer probability of magic is always higher.<br /> My own idea is walked on. And is omniscience possible?<br /> Question is not in dice pool or paradox recoil - we can come up with a scheme where they will be optimal so much that if it were allowed, it would be possible. Anyway, we assume that the head of one of the Orders is looking for a beginners (ie 7-9 dots in Gnosis and Mastery of Arcanes allowed). The problem of the objective reasons why it can not happen. As in principle omniscience and search of novices in particular.<br /> <br /> My point here besides the obvious opponents (whom would distract caster or disspell his magic) there would be the following factors. At firs particular in novices' search task we will only see not person himself but his own Nimbus or Resonances of his spells. And Resonance of his spells will contain his Nimbus. There we will not distinguish between sorcery and wizard himself. And the task is complicated by the probability of sympathetic spells. In second spells which has not yet happened is not affect the possibility of magic.<br /> That is in addition to ubiquity (the ability to look under every stone), you need to have more understanding of things. Depending on the point of view of a character can possess it, or may not possess. In the description of practice, the first points give the so-called &quot;Understanding&quot;. Depending on the latitude of interpretation, we can really assume that omniscience rests on dicepool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-24-2017, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:05:19-08:00","id":1037385,"title":"","content":"Having problems parsing the text, but is your question about detecting new (rare) Mages? If so, Fate magic might get you close enough to do some more targeted Prime detection. Do Proximi fill in the &quot;gap&quot; (IE, are there far more Proximi, with only a few full Mages)? If so, perhaps there is at least one &quot;witch-finder&quot; Dynasty that head-hunts newly Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-